# Documentation > Source code style guide > Structs and enums > Formatting of struct fields and enum variants

Formatting of struct fields and enum variants

Add newlines to struct fields and enum variants when they include additional information like documentation comments or attributes, because the variants can become difficult to read.
This is especially the case when fields include doc comments, attributes like#[snafu()], and in case of enum variants, various embedded types.

Enum variants and struct fields don’t need to be separated whennoadditional information is attached to any of the variants or fields.

[TIP] enum Color {
    Red,
    Green,
    Blue,
}

struct Foo {
    /// My doc comment for bar
    bar: usize,

    /// My doc comment for baz
    baz: usize,
}

enum Error {
    /// Indicates that we failed to foo.
    #[snafu(display("failed to foo"))]
    Foo,

    /// Indicates that we failed to bar.
    #[snafu(display("failed to bar"))]
    Bar,
    Baz,
}

Communication between NiFi nodes

To allow communication between NiFi nodes an additional rego rule is required:


[CODE BLOCK]


allow := {
  "allowed": true
} if {
  input.identity.name == "CN=generated certificate for pod" (1)
  input.resource.id == "/proxy" (2)
}


[/CODE BLOCK]



[CODE BLOCK]
allow := {
  "allowed": true
} if {
  input.identity.name == "CN=generated certificate for pod" (1)
  input.resource.id == "/proxy" (2)
}
[/CODE BLOCK]


1 | The identity of NiFi nodes authenticated with TLS certificates provided by the secrets operator.
2 | Only access to the/proxyAPI is required.

Expiration date

Annotation: restarter.stackable.tech/expires-at.{tag}

restarter.stackable.tech/expires-at.{tag}

Pods can be configured to expire at a certain point in time.
In this case, the Pod should have the annotationrestarter.stackable.tech/expires-at.{tag}set to a datetime formatted according to RFC 3339 (such as"2022-04-21T13:24:15.225774724+00:00").{tag}should be a deterministic but unique ID identifying the reason for the expiry.

Multipleexpires-atannotations can be set on the same Pod, in which case theearliestexpiration datetime takes precedence.

Caching

